root_cause:
The validation step was never implemented. src/entities/commands.zig `createRecord()` carries it as a literal TODO, lines ~103-104:

    // 2. TODO: Validate field_values against definition.definition_json
    // For EXP-202 Stage 1, we assume JSON is valid or validated upstream.

The definition IS loaded immediately above (definition_mod.getDefinitionByName) and `definition.definition_json` is in hand, but nothing compares `params.field_values` against it. `EntityCommandError.InvalidPayload` is declared in the error set and is documented as the outcome for this case, but no code path in src/entities/ ever returns it.

`updateRecord()` has the same gap — it loads the definition and builds the updated payload without validating field_values against it.

The assumption recorded in the comment ("validated upstream") does not hold: the command functions are called directly by the REST route handlers and by tests, with no intervening validation layer. src/entities/validator.zig validates entity DEFINITIONS (the schema), not entity RECORDS (instances of that schema) — the record-level validator does not exist.
